{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And ships from the coast of Kittim.</b> After he mentioned that Asshur would afflict the Kenite, he now says that a time would come when Asshur and Eber would be punished — the meaning is the Hebrews whom Asshur afflicted — for the Kittim would rule over Israel. And 'ships' (וצים) is plural, from the expression (Isaiah 33:21) ״וצי אדיר״. And Kittim is of the descendants of Javan, and it is possible that it is an allusion to the wicked kingdom of Ishmael." "<b>And know that</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, held that Kittim is Rome, and it is the kingdom of Edom, which is the fourth beast. And so he concluded this prophecy of his, which is the fourth, with the destruction of Kittim, which is Rome, and it is the fourth beast concerning which Daniel prophesied (Daniel 7:11) ״עד די קטילת חיותא והובד גשמה ויהיבת ליקידת אשא״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:53.500010699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}